    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What is the best time to do the Spiti group trip?",
        "answer": "We run this trip from November through winter on the Shimla–Kinnaur route. November brings clear skies and the first snow, and from mid-December to mid-March the valley is fully snow-covered with frozen waterfalls."
      },
      {
        "question": "Where does the Spiti group trip start and end?",
        "answer": "It starts and ends in Delhi. You board an overnight Volvo / AC semi-sleeper from Delhi to Shimla on the evening of Day 1 and arrive back in Delhi early on the morning of Day 9."
      },
      {
        "question": "How much does the Spiti group trip from Delhi cost?",
        "answer": "₹17,499 per person on quad sharing and ₹18,499 on triple sharing, plus 5% GST. This covers Delhi–Shimla–Delhi transit, a dedicated Tempo Traveller, 6 nights' stay, 12 meals, permits and a trip captain."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is Spiti Valley open in winter?",
        "answer": "Yes. The Shimla–Kinnaur route that this trip follows stays open through winter. The Manali side over Kunzum Pass closes for the season, which is why winter Spiti trips go via Kinnaur."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I join the Spiti group trip solo?",
        "answer": "Yes, solo travellers are welcome. Rooms are on a sharing basis with fellow travellers from the group."
      },
      {
        "question": "How cold does it get in Spiti during winter?",
        "answer": "Daytime temperatures range between -5°C and 5°C, while nighttime temperatures drop significantly between -15°C and -25°C."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is this trip suitable for beginners or first-time travelers?",
        "answer": "Yes, beginners in good health can join, provided they strictly follow winter layering guidelines and allow time for proper altitude acclimatization."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do we cope with High Altitude Sickness (AMS)?",
        "answer": "Stay well hydrated, avoid alcohol or smoking, ascend gradually, and keep our expedition leader informed immediately if you feel dizzy or nauseous. Backup oxygen cylinders and basic medical kits are carried with the group."
      },
      {
        "question": "Will running water and electricity be available in winter?",
        "answer": "Due to sub-zero temperatures, pipelines freeze throughout Spiti. Traditional dry toilets (compost pits) and warm water in buckets are provided at homestays, and power cuts can occur during heavy snowfall."
      },
      {
        "question": "What kind of clothing and gear should I pack?",
        "answer": "Pack 3-4 warm thermal base layers, fleece jackets, a windproof and waterproof down feather jacket (-20°C rated), waterproof snow shoes with good grip, woolen socks, gloves, a balaclava, UV-protection sunglasses, and high-SPF sunscreen."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are room heaters included in the package?",
        "answer": "Room heaters are not included in the standard package due to remote power constraints; where available, properties may charge an additional fee directly based on electricity or generator use."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which mobile network works best in Kinnaur and Spiti?",
        "answer": "Postpaid Jio and BSNL networks offer the most consistent connectivity in Sangla, Kalpa, and Kaza. Airtel works intermittently, and most prepaid connections from outside Himachal lose signal beyond Reckong Peo."
      },
      {
        "question": "What happens if the roads get blocked due to heavy snowfall?",
        "answer": "Winter Himalayan routes can face delays from snowstorms or roadblocks. The itinerary includes buffer planning, and our experienced captains and mountain drivers coordinate safe route adjustments or alternate halts as required."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I get pure vegetarian or Jain food during the tour?",
        "answer": "Yes, wholesome, freshly cooked vegetarian meals are served across all designated stays, and basic Jain food preferences can be accommodated if informed prior to departure."
      }
    ],
