    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What is the \"Trail Explorers\" experience all about?",
        "answer": "We aren't a traditional travel agency; we are a community. Our trips focus on slow travel, local stories, and building a \"hype squad\" on the road. Expect raw beauty, offbeat trails, and a group of strangers who leave as family."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is there an age limit for the trips?",
        "answer": "Our typical tribe consists of travelers aged 18 to 35. We curate our itineraries for those who enjoy high-energy exploration, shared stays, and a bit of adventure."
      },
      {
        "question": "I’m a solo traveler. Is it safe for me?",
        "answer": "Absolutely! A large percentage of our explorers join solo. Safety—especially for solo female travelers—is our top priority. Our Trip Captains are trained to ensure a secure and inclusive environment for everyone."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I book my spot?",
        "answer": "To lock your seat, you only need to pay a 10% non-refundable token amount. The remaining balance can be settled comfortably upon your arrival at the starting point of the trip."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the cancellation policy?",
        "answer": "The 10% booking token is non-refundable as it goes toward securing your permits and stay. For cancellations of the remaining amount, please refer to our detailed Terms & Conditions page."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the role of a Trip Captain?",
        "answer": "Your Trip Captain is your storyteller, logistics manager, and resident photographer. They aren’t just guides; they are part of the group, ensuring everything runs smoothly while keeping the energy high."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are adventure activities (Paragliding, Rafting, ATV) included?",
        "answer": "While we help facilitate these experiences at the best local rates, adventure activities are typically not included in the base package price. This allows you the flexibility to choose only the thrills you want!"
      },
      {
        "question": "What happens in case of bad weather or roadblocks?",
        "answer": "In the mountains, nature calls the shots. In case of Force Majeure (landslides, heavy snow, or government restrictions), we will try our best to provide an alternative plan. However, any additional costs arising from such situations are to be borne by the traveler."
      },
      {
        "question": "What should I pack for Kashmir?",
        "answer": "Layers are your best friend! Even in summer, nights can be chilly. For winter trips, heavy woolens, thermal wear, and waterproof shoes are a must. We will send a detailed packing checklist to your WhatsApp group before the trip."
      },
      {
        "question": "Will I have network connectivity?",
        "answer": "In remote areas like parts of Kashmir, connectivity can be patchy. We recommend carrying a postpaid SIM (BSNL or Airtel usually work best). Think of it as a \"digital detox\"—the best connections are the ones made with people, not towers!"
      }
    ],
