      {
        "question": "How difficult is the Tungnath-Chandrashila trek?",
        "answer": "It is easy-to-moderate and perfect for first-timers! The trail to Tungnath is well-paved, with a steeper last 1.5 km to Chandrashila summit."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the best time for this trip?",
        "answer": "Winter (Dec–Feb) for snow and skiing, Spring/Summer (Mar–Jun) for blooming meadows, and Autumn (Oct–Nov) for clear peak views."
      },
      {
        "question": "I don't know how to swim. Can I still do River Rafting in Rishikesh?",
        "answer": "Yes, high-buoyancy life jackets and helmets are provided along with professional guide briefings."
      },
      {
        "question": "What kind of stays should I expect?",
        "answer": "Hostels/riverside camps in Rishikesh, Swiss tents/cottages in Chopta, and homestays/guesthouses in Auli/Joshimath."
      },
      {
        "question": "Will I get mobile network and electricity in Chopta?",
        "answer": "Network is patchy (Jio/BSNL work best) and electricity is solar-limited. Carrying a 20,000mAh power bank is recommended."
      },
      {
        "question": "What should I pack for Chopta/Auli?",
        "answer": "3-layer clothing (thermal, fleece, waterproof jacket), sturdy trekking shoes, sunscreen, lip balm, and a reusable water bottle."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is there an ATM available?",
        "answer": "ATMs are available in Rishikesh and Joshimath, but NOT in Chopta or Auli. Carry sufficient cash."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do we travel between these places?",
        "answer": "Comfortable high-clearance vehicles like Bolero, Scorpio, or Tempo Traveler suited for mountain roads."
      },
      {
        "question": "What if I get Altitude Sickness (AMS)?",
        "answer": "The itinerary is paced for acclimatization and Trip Captains carry first-aid kits. Stay hydrated and avoid heavy meals."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I join solo?",
        "answer": "Yes! Most travelers join solo and are paired with same-gender roommates/tentmates."
      }
